## Telegram Integration

### New Command: `/grunt`

Update [brain_telegram.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/brain_telegram.py) (which runs on Render) to use GitHub Issues.

```python
# In brain_telegram.py

from github import Github  # or use requests/subprocess if simpler, but pygithub is cleaner
import os

def handle_grunt_command(task_description: str) -> str:
    """Handle /grunt <task description> command."""
    if not task_description:
        return "❌ Usage: /grunt Create mood chart widget"
    
    try:
        # Create GitHub Issue
        # Note: Requires GITHUB_TOKEN env var on Render
        g = Github(os.getenv("GITHUB_TOKEN"))
        repo = g.get_repo("lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend")  # Hardcoded for now
        issue = repo.create_issue(
            title=f"Grunt: {task_description[:50]}...",
            body=task_description,
            labels=["grunt-work"]
        )
        
        return f"🔧 Grunt task queued!\n\nIssue #{issue.number}\nTask: {task_description[:50]}\n\nWorker will pick this up."
    except Exception as e:
        return f"❌ Failed to queue task: {str(e)}"
```

